## Calling an endpoint

Every route requires a bearer token; `/health` does not.

```bash
TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST http://localhost:[[ port ]]/auth/dev-token \
  -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{"subject":"local-run"}' \
  | sed -n 's/.*"access_token":"\([^"]*\)".*/\1/p')

curl -s http://localhost:[[ port ]]/health
```

`POST /auth/dev-token` exists only in development mode (set by the compose file) and is never
available in a deployed instance, which validates Microsoft Entra ID tokens instead.
